# Battle Targeting System

## Initial Target Selection
### Priority Order
1. Neutral nodes within network line
2. Enemy battalions within range
3. Defensive positions (Guardians only)

### Line Restrictions
- Battalions can only target within their assigned network line
- No targeting across different network lines
- Must respect initial line assignments throughout battle

## Battalion-Specific Targeting
### Guardian Targeting
- Prioritize maintaining control of current node
- Target neutral nodes for capture
- Defend nearest controlled node if no neutral targets
- Do not attempt to recapture enemy nodes

### Breacher/Phreak Targeting
- Prioritize capturing neutral nodes
- Avoid targeting recently captured nodes
- Target enemy battalions if no neutral nodes available
- Sort potential targets by distance

## Combat Range
### Range Calculation
- Calculate from battalion center to target center
- Position at edge of attack range
- Account for target size and type
- Maintain minimum safe distance

### Attack Positioning
- Calculate optimal attack position
- Stay within network line constraints
- Account for other battalions' positions
- Update position if target moves

## Retargeting Logic
### Trigger Conditions
- Current target destroyed
- Node captured
- Target moves out of range
- Better target becomes available

### Retargeting Rules
- Respect network line restrictions
- Follow battalion-specific priorities
- Avoid ping-pong targeting
- Consider cooldown periods

## Combat Sequence
### Attack Initiation
- Verify target is in range
- Check line of sight
- Validate attack permissions
- Start attack animation

### Combat Flow
- Calculate damage
- Apply effects
- Update health states
- Trigger visual feedback

## Performance Considerations
### Optimization
- Efficient target validation
- Quick range calculations
- Smooth targeting transitions
- Proper resource management

### Error Handling
- Handle invalid targets
- Manage targeting failures
- Log targeting issues
- Implement fallback logic

Remember: Targeting must respect network line restrictions and battalion-specific priorities while maintaining system performance. 